<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The native contract (spec R-09-123): the one assembly between the runtime image and the native activities a distribution
    carries. Its Version is the contract version. A distribution's manifest names the version its native assemblies were built
    against, and the runtime takes the major it supports at a minor no later than its own (NativeContract.Supports). A type a
    module could see that is added here is a new minor; one changed or removed is a new major. Keep NativeContract.Version the same.
    1.1.0 (R-09-125, Issue I-220): INativeServices gives core banking, the bank's other ports, the host's files and the contributions
    of the other modules of the distribution, so a module references this assembly and no other of TransactHub.
    2.0.0 (R-09-261 to R-09-264, Issues I-315, I-226): bound ports (INativeServices.BoundPorts), so a module builds the adapters of its
    own scheme's ports; a module's gate on a binding (NativeBindingGate); Service<T> is removed, so a 1.x module is refused
    (native.ContractUnsupported). Every module is rebuilt against it (docs/runtime/PACKAGING-AND-DEPLOYMENT.md section 3.2).
    2.1.0 (R-09-276 to R-09-281, Issues I-382, I-383): a minor. A balance enquiry on a core-banking binding (INativeCoreBankingBinding.Balance),
    so the reservation, its release, the reversal and the check of a posting are the platform module's; and on the bound ports a body
    of bytes with its content type (NativeHttpRequest.Content) and a file put through the binding's transfer (INativeBoundPorts.Put).
    A 2.0 module runs on it unchanged; a 2.1 module on a 2.0 runtime is refused (native.ContractUnsupported).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <Version>2.1.0</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>2.1.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>2.1.0.0</FileVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
